---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title={`About`} description="About this site and its author.">
	<div class="flex min-h-[calc(100dvh-4rem)] flex-col items-center px-6 py-6 md:py-16">
		<main class="w-full max-w-[600px]">
			<div class="py-4">
				<h1 class="font-serif text-[48px] leading-tight text-ink">
					About<span class="opacity-40">.</span>
				</h1>
			</div>
			<div class="mb-8 h-px bg-bd"></div>
			<p class="font-sans text-[15px] leading-[1.8] text-ink-80">
				I’m a computer engineering student at Warwick. The site is built with Astro and is a place
				to keep my{' '}<a
					href="/writings"
					class="underline decoration-ink/20 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-ink"
					>writings</a
				>, collect things I like, and share what I’m working on.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-5 font-sans text-[15px] leading-[1.8] text-ink-80">
				I’m a fan of history, particularly the <a
					href="/writing/de-hooch-vermeer"
					class="underline decoration-ink/20 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-ink"
					>Dutch Golden Age painters</a
				>, and of art more broadly, with a bias towards French Classicism, Romanticism, and the
				Hague School. I edit Wikipedia, especially aforementioned topics, as much as I have time
				for. I’m fond of cartography, or any good information graphic for that matter. I read mostly
				the classics, and even more so the works of postwar Japan, such as Mishima, Seichō
				Matsumoto, or Murakami. I’m nowhere near as knowledgeable in <a
					href="/writing/philosophical-credo"
					class="underline decoration-ink/20 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-ink"
					>philosophy</a
				> as I’d like to be, but I’ve read Sartre, Nietzsche, Voltaire, Mill, Hume, and the like. I care
				about <a
					href="/writing/rent-control"
					class="underline decoration-ink/20 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-ink"
					>politics</a
				>, too, because I hate the normalisation of dysfunctional systems.
			</p>
		</main>
		<figure class="mt-10 w-full max-w-[600px]">
			<img
				src="/friedrich-monk-by-the-sea.webp"
				alt="The Monk by the Sea, by Caspar David Friedrich"
				width="720"
				height="458"
				style="aspect-ratio: 720 / 458"
				class="h-auto w-full rounded-sm object-cover"
				loading="lazy"
			/>
			<figcaption class="mt-5 text-center font-mono text-[12px] leading-relaxed text-ink-80">
				Caspar David Friedrich – The Monk by the Sea, c. 1808–10
			</figcaption>
		</figure>
		<div class="w-full max-w-[600px]">
			<Footer />
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
